ing=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(A) Over all order of this reaction is one.</p>\n<p>(B) Order of this reaction can't be determined.</p>\n<p>(C) In region I and III, the reaction is of first and zero order respectively.</p>\n<p>(D) In region-II, the reaction is of first order.</p>\n<p>(E) In region-II, the order of reaction is in the range of 0.1 to 0.9.</p>",
      "options": [],
      "correct_options": [],
      "explanation": "<p>In region I and II, slope of the graph is positive so reaction is nagative order.</p>\n<p>In region III, slope of the graph is zero so the reaction is of zero order.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Order of this reaction can't be determined. So only (B) is correct.</p>"
